WEBVTT

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.360
This is Chad Huntley.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.320
Changed immeasurably.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.350
Weather-beaten mud paths have turned into vast highway system.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.240
A Pony Express rider has been replaced with telephone wires.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.120
And small flames that used to light our way have turned into electric giants.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.300
Changed as well.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:29.960
Town crime.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.860
voices have been replaced by the sharp hit of a newspaper against the back door.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.550
The hoofbeats of horses have been changed into motors and horns, and the

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:45.300
sound of an aircraft engine is now a jet whine. The producers of this report, in

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.940
cooperation with headquarters, United States Air Force, and the Strategic Air

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:54.460
Command, want you to know about a new sound, what causes it, what it can and

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:59.980
cannot do, and why it will be necessary for certain populated areas to live with

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.800
Unless we learn to live with it, we may not live at all.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:32.580
Thank you.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:18.280
A geographical center of the continental United States, known as the Great Plains Area.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:23.670
Here near Omaha, in the seemingly illogical surroundings of miles of farmland,

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.420
is the headquarters of a major deterrent strength of this country.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:29.970
Headquarters, Strategic Air...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.220
Command, the organization responsible for implementing the philosophy, the policy of

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:35.820
deterrence.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.980
As the book says, the mission of the Strategic Air Command is to be prepared to conduct strategic

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:48.420
air operations on a global basis, so that in the event of sudden aggression, SAC could

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:54.090
immediately mount simultaneous nuclear attacks designed to destroy the vital elements of

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.480
the aggressor's war-making capability, to the extent that he would no longer have the

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.970
will nor ability.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:10.760
to wage war. From this headquarters building near Omaha, Nebraska, the commander-in-chief can order

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:18.220
SAC's combat-ready alert bombers into the air in a matter of seconds. 24 hours a day, every day,

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:23.940
from SAC bases throughout the world. From the North American Air Defense Command, information

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.980
is fed into the control center to be correlated on these panels. Information vital to the direct...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.870
of the strike force. Already charted on the panels behind the drapes are SAC's emergency war plans,

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:44.490
plans detailing each target for every plane, every missile in the SAC arsenal. Should war ever come,

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:50.230
the curtains would be drawn aside. In a matter of moments, the control center would be sealed off

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.890
in fighting configuration.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:17.720
When the receiver of the red telephone is picked up, every SAC base in the world could hear the words that would signal an alert, and the most powerful strike force that has ever been seen would be unleashed.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:27.920
The gold telephone is in readiness for only one phone call, to relay the most vital order from the President of the United States to the Commander-in-Chief of SAC.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:37.680
Skybird, this is Dropkick to all stations.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.960
All stations acknowledge at the count of five.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.800
One, two, three, four, and five.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:59.210
This is Dropkick releasing the alerting system.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:13.040
Each day and night, the Strategic Air Command continues to rehearse for a mission it hopes it will never be called upon to perform.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:19.110
Rehearsals directed in this underground room go on all over the United States.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.870
Most of the time, our country is unaware of these rehearsals.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.900
They don't interfere with our normal, everyday way of life, but occasionally, this is not true.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:37.300
become very much aware that we are engaged in the new art of deterrent defense. But this

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:42.600
sound, which can be louder than thunder, is only a pin-dropping compared to a possible

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:53.940
alternative. In this hideous cloud is a revolution in military strategy, an entirely new philosophy

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:59.940
of international relations. Standing in awe before it, free men realize that the secret

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.080
this incredible new weapon could not be held for long.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.320
That soon the arsenals of governments dedicated to world domination

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:12.280
would be stockpiled with bombs that would make this one look like a firecracker.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.870
And they knew then that to protect themselves from the bomb

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.470
and from the ambition of totalitarian states,

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:22.210
they must build a military striking force so strong

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:24.980
that to provoke it would be suicidal.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.440
And so the strategy of deterrence was born.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.840
through the foreseeable future, SAC will be equipped with planes as well as missiles.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.030
At present, more than one half dozen different types of missiles have been integrated into

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:15.080
the SAC arsenal, with more to be added as rapidly as they become operationally reliable.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.860
The first intercontinental ballistic missile to take its place in the deterrent force is

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:26.490
the Atlas, but missiles are not yet available in sufficient quantities to be more than an

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.980
adjunct to the deterrent force and there is

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.700
another problem. In the event of a surprise attack launched against us, the long-range radar of our

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:41.510
early warning system might give us no more than 15 minutes warning. In those 15 minutes, we would

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:47.290
have to get our retaliatory strike force in the air or face the possibility of having it wiped out

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:54.380
on the ground. If our deterrent force consisted solely of missiles, every ready weapon would have

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:59.820
to be launched at once. But the problem is that at the present time, our high frequency

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.720
long-range radar is still subject to many bugs, electronic disturbances, interference from other

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:12.620
radar installations. Even flights of birds can create patterns on the radar screen that could

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.490
be mistaken for an attacking force. Checking and rechecking could well use up those precious 15

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:26.070
minutes. As long as there is any doubt, we dare not launch our missiles. For once fired and on its way

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:29.350
to target. An ICBM cannot be called back.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:31.210
Bombers can.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:37.420
The newest manned weapon in SAC's arsenal to maintain the peace

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:41.840
is the supersonic Delta Wing B-58 Hustler Jet Bomber.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:55.280
One jump, the B-58, built by the Convair Division of General Dynamics,

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:59.150
powered by General Electric J-79 turbojet engines,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.040
has outstripped the past 50 years of aviation history.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:07.360
Top speed is as much faster than the speediest previous bomber,

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:11.970
as that plane was faster than the Wright Brothers' original flying machine.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:36.650
A philosophy, an organization, modern weapons, and then men.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:43.930
Trained men to fly these weapon systems, trained by practice of bombing missions, without bombs.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:51.780
Directed by SAC, a practice bombing mission, one of thousands, is to be sent from Carswell Air Force Base in Fort Worth, Texas,

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:55.620
where the top flight SAC bomber crews are undergoing training.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.360
Please get the Excel points.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.360
Okay, acceleration.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:09:59.790
We're going to ask feedback.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.060
This crew has almost completed its indoctrination course in the B-58 Hustler.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:09.890
Only a few blanks remain to be filled out on their performance record charts

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:15.350
before they will be qualified as a combat-ready crew in the free world's fastest bomber.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:20.560
They are the aircraft commander and pilot, Major Joseph E. Briggs.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:25.870
Aged 38, 14 years with the Air Force, married, four children.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.470
You're going to be specified, is that correct?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.810
Mirage completed.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:37.340
Systems Officer, Captain William H. Scanlon. Age 31, 10 years in the Air Force, married, three children.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:46.500
Navigator, Captain Walter C. Lyles. Age 30, six years in the Air Force, married, one child.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:55.260
Each SAC training mission is planned with painstaking care. For every hour they will spend

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:58.860
in the air, one and one-half hours have been spent in preparation on the ground.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.900
Each mile is literally flown on paper before it's flown in the sky.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:09.930
They say in SAC that you're not ready to take off until the weight of the paper equals the weight of the aircraft.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.400
This will be a radar bombing.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:17.130
The target, a long-range one, routed over 3,000 miles away,

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.400
the center of the village square, Deerfield, Massachusetts.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.780
which is a quiet New England village,

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.540
has a history of hearing the sounds of freedom's battles.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.980
And the memory of those sounds has been preserved in a memorial.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.240
One morning in 1704,

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.060
50 of Deerfield's residents were killed and hundreds taken away as prisoners.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.280
Half the city was burned to the ground.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.550
Again, in our country's revolution,

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.970
and in the ensuing years, Deerfield heard...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.140
the sounds necessary to protect their freedom. Now Deerfield had been chosen again. This time

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:12.130
there would be no battle attack, no fires, no explosions, but there would be a sound,

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:18.800
a sound of protection loud enough to be heard by every resident in the village. Deerfield had not

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:24.920
been chosen arbitrarily. This city, along with many other radar bomb sites or targets in the

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:29.750
United States, was carefully selected because the pattern it makes in the plane's radar

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:29.790
Bye.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:29.890
Bye.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.880
is similar to that of an actual target in potential enemy territory.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:38.900
The relation of the buildings, the hills, and the houses,

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.410
even the memorial of Deerfield creates a similar radar pattern

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:46.060
to a possible enemy target city.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:50.920
The bomb they drop on the American target is a harmless electronic beam.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.260
It would, of course, be something else

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.400
if they were flying in anger to a target beyond our borders.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.920
To reach their radar bomb-scoring sight target,

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:05.610
the SAC crews fly a roundabout course over the United States of several thousand miles

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:08.630
to approximate the distance to their actual target.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:13.380
During the latter stages of the flight, they may engage in evasive tactics

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.220
against U.S. fighter planes of our Air Defense Command,

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:20.470
testing their ability to penetrate any possible enemy defense.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.940
Refueling to the south tip of Coates Island, then on up north,

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.670
back to Coates Island, to our HR control line.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:37.750
our start acceleration point, to our turn point on Lake Huron, to our IP in Lake Ontario,

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:46.970
to target echo Deerfield, to our turn point, Nashville, Tennessee, Carswell, let down and land.

